							<span class="meta-cats m-l-lg">Category:  <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/category/new-product-reviews/" rel="category tag">New Product Reviews</a>, <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/category/product-guides/" rel="category tag">Product Guides</a></span>
			
			
			
			
			
												<span class="post-date-block m-l-lg">
						<span>Post Date: </span><span class="font-weight-semibold">September 9, 2026</span>
					</span>
									</div>
		<hr class="solid">
						<div class="entry-content">
			<p>The Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol with Blowback is one of those rare air pistols that gets everything right: licensed Glock authenticity, a proper blowback slide, and the accuracy advantage of a rifled barrel firing .177 pellets. If you have been eyeing the Glock range and wondering which model of all our <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/">Airguns</a> is the one to buy, this is our pick — and here is why.</p>
<h2>First Impressions</h2>
<p>Out of the box, the first thing you notice is the weight: 830 grams of polymer and metal in a 1:1 scale body measuring 202mm. It feels exactly like the real Glock 17 should, with the Gen5 detail work all present — the front serrations, the reversible magazine release button, the trigger safety, and the generously sized grip. The official licensed Glock markings are crisp, and the finish is flawless.</p>
<h2>Performance</h2>
<p>This is where the Gen5 pellet version separates itself from the BB-firing Glocks in the range. Instead of steel BBs, it feeds 4.5mm (.177) pellets from its 21-round magazine by means of a chain — a clever system that keeps pellets seated securely and feeds reliably shot after shot. Because pellets engage the rifled barrel properly, groupings are noticeably tighter than you get from a smoothbore BB shooter, and that makes every range session more satisfying.</p>
<p>Power comes from a single 12g CO2 cartridge housed in the magazine, delivering around 3J (roughly 394 FPS) in semi-auto. The blowback action kicks the slide back with every shot, giving a strong, snappy recoil impulse that makes target shooting genuinely fun. You get the realism of the slide cycling with the precision of pellet shooting — the best of both worlds. It slots neatly alongside the other <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/air-pistols/">Air Pistols</a> we stock.</p>
<h2><img decoding="async" class="alignnone" src="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/glock17gen5-review-bench.jpg" alt="Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol on a bench" width="" height="" /></h2>
<h2>Build Quality</h2>
<p>Construction is a sensible polymer/metal mix: the frame is tough polymer that shrugs off knocks, while the slide and internals bring the metal weight that sells the blowback feel. The double/single action trigger is crisp, the manual safety is positive, and the drop-free style magazine is easy to load and change. Being a licensed Umarex <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/glock-17-gen5-co2-pellet-air-pistol/">Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol</a> replica, everything lines up with aftermarket holsters too — a nice bonus if you like to store or transport it properly.</p>
<h2><img decoding="async" class="alignnone" src="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/glock17gen5-review-range.jpg" alt="Shooting the Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol at an indoor range" width="" height="" /></h2>
<h2>In the Box and Specifications</h2>
<p>You get the pistol, the 21-round magazine, a CO2 installation tool, and the manual. Key specs:</p>
<ul>
<li>Calibre: .177 (4.5mm) pellet</li>
<li>Power: 12g CO2</li>
<li>Energy: 3J / approx. 394 FPS</li>
<li>Magazine: 21 rounds, chain-fed</li>
<li>Action: semi-auto, double/single, blowback</li>
<li>Construction: polymer / metal</li>
<li>Length: 202mm; Weight: 830g</li>
<li>Safety: manual; 1:1 scale licensed replica</li>
</ul>
<h2><img decoding="async" class="alignnone" src="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/glock17gen5-review-flatlay.jpg" alt="Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol flat-lay with magazine and CO2 capsule" width="" height="" /></h2>
<h2>Who Is It For?</h2>
<p>This is a pistol for the target and plinking shooter who wants realism and accuracy in one package. If you enjoy precise shot placement and a satisfying recoil cycle, the pellet-fed Gen5 is the Glock to choose. As with all airguns sold by <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/">Airguns</a>, sales are strictly to persons aged 18 and over in line with the VCR Act 2006, and this pistol is intended for safe target shooting on private land or at a range.</p>
<h2>Verdict</h2>
<p>The Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol with Blowback is, in our opinion, the best Glock in the air pistol line-up: licensed looks, real blowback, and pellet accuracy that BB versions simply cannot match. At £214.99 it is a premium air pistol, but the build and shooting experience justify every penny. Browse the full range in our <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/air-pistols/">Air Pistols</a> category.</p>
<p>Check out the <a href="https://www.justairguns.co.uk/glock-17-gen5-co2-pellet-air-pistol/">Glock 17 Gen5 CO2 Pellet Air Pistol</a> on the product page.</p>
